---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Us — ClipU"
	description="ClipU is a free online YouTube video cutter for trimming and downloading MP4 or MP3 clips, no login required."
>
	<main class="bg-canvas-soft text-ink font-sans">
		<div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 pt-20 pb-16">
			<h1 class="text-[32px] font-semibold leading-10 tracking-[-1.28px] text-center">About ClipU</h1>

			<div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-5 text-base text-body leading-7">
				<p>
					ClipU is a free online YouTube video cutter built around one job: turning a YouTube link
					into the exact clip you need, as fast as possible. Paste a link, trim to the moment that
					matters, and download it as MP4 or MP3 — no software to install, no account to create.
				</p>
				<p>
					We built it because most tools that call themselves a "YouTube video cutter online"
					bury the actual trimming behind sign-up walls, watermarks, or a queue of ads before the
					download link shows up. ClipU skips all of that. There's no plan to upgrade to and no
					feature locked behind a login — the free version is the only version.
				</p>
				<p>
					It's aimed at anyone who needs a specific moment out of a longer video: video editors
					pulling reference clips, marketers grabbing a quotable ten seconds, students saving a
					segment of a lecture, or anyone who just wants a song's audio from a YouTube link without
					downloading the whole video first.
				</p>
				<p>
					ClipU doesn't keep accounts, doesn't store your clips after they're downloaded, and
					doesn't track what you cut. See our <a href="/privacy-policy" class="text-link hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>
					for the details, or the <a href="/terms-and-conditions" class="text-link hover:underline">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>
					for how the service is meant to be used.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="mt-14 flex justify-center">
				<a
					href="/"
					class="rounded-pill bg-ink text-on-primary px-5 h-10 inline-flex items-center text-base font-medium hover:opacity-90"
				>
					Try it now
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</main>
</Layout>
